            <ArticleTitle>Electrocatalytic Dehydrogenative Esterification of Aliphatic Carboxylic Acids: Access to Bioactive Lactones.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6622-6625</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b03333</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A scalable and efficient electrocatalytic dehydrogenative esterification is reported. With an indirect electrolysis strategy, both intra- and intermolecular-type reactions were amenable to this practical method. With n-Bu4NI as the catalyst, undesired decarboxylation and Baeyer-Villiger oxidation were suppressed. More importantly, this novel method provided reliable and direct access to the natural product cytosporanone A on a gram scale.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
